k or want or you want as a master, if the players summons an aspect of the incarna/Celestine to learn a gift, is very easy to treat it like something shrouded in mistery and mysticism and in some books are described what the scions of the celestine looks like and they're behaviour - For example Febe, scion of Luna, and yes I know I'm using scion in an incorrect manner, sorry, or simply a simple lune.<br /> <br /> In the matters of the Celestine/Incarna in direct contact with the player without intermediaries...<br /> As a master, in the next session my players will encounter Fenris and his two lil brothers, Cerunnos, Stag and Ratatoshk in a very heated discussion about Pegasus who is dying at they're feet.<br /> I'm gonna roleplaying them without the mistery of the mistycism, they are the real thing not shrouden in anything: For example, Fenris is all buddy buddy, informal and party loving, and his most inner desire is to see Luna and Helios very dead, boasting it in every opportunity he had and Stag is a snobbish bastard who doesn't like having his hoofs dirty... Pegasus is a half plushie hobby horse.<br /> <br /> What i'm try to say with all of that is, - lessening the fact that I'm mastering a very heretic chronicle - is it doesn't matters what the vision of a god his people have, it's nothing more of a interpretation of it basing of it's own perception of the being not the being itself, It doesn't matter if Fenris is seeing as an avatar of destruction, in his intimacy he can do whatever he wants, even if it's sponsoring the best raves in all the umbra.<br /> My Gaia is madly in love with the Wyrm, Eshtarra is the embodiment of the Wyrm prission and the Weaver is making New Phyrexia with the Scar, Helios is an infinity of lesser Aspects being known as Helios, and Helios is also Helios himself...<br /> <br /> Really, for a master to ask something like this... what part of do whatever you want you don't understand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img i